Columns (Serial No. / Rank): 1 IG Prisons | 2 DIG | 3 AIG Prisons/ Senior Superintendent | 4 Superintendent | 4 Superintendent with 2 years Service | 5 Deputy Superintendent | 6 Assistant Superintendent | 7 Sub Inspector | 8 Assistant Sub Inspector | 9 Head Constable | 10 Senior Prison Constable | 11 Prison Constable

Jacket — cols 1–6: Grey drill serge or Grey Bush Jacket /Service Dress (SD) Jacket, fabric suiting the climatic conditions, Sam Browne or removable waist belt with buckle, buttoned cuffs, turned down collars, medium prison-pattern buttons down the front, four front pockets with plain flaps to buttons, shoulder straps plain fastening at top with a small prison-pattern button, Shoulder Ranks, Gorget Patches of pattern approved for substantive rank (gorget patches cols 1–3 only), [shoulder] Letters "SPCS", name plate, national flag, medals or medal ribbons, as the case may be. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria.

Raincoat — cols 1–6: Navy Blue, long below knees, hooded, water-proof fabric, four front pockets, "SPCS" inscription on the front left pocket and middle of upper back. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria with SPCS inscription.

Jersey — cols 1–6: Grey, woolen, full sleeves, V-Neck, two breast pockets with plain flaps to buttons, shoulder straps, police/military pattern. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria.

Cap — cols 1–6: Navy Blue Beret, Black Woolen Roll-Over Winter Cap, Navy Blue Pole Cap or Navy Blue Peaked Cap with blue band around, police /military pattern, with cap badge. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria.

Cap Badge — col 1: Silver colour, embroidered, national emblem on the top, floral circlet, crossed sword and baton inside as prescribed for Major General of the Pakistan Army; col 2: Silver colour, embroidered, floral circlet crescent containing a five-points star inside as prescribed for Brigadier of the Pakistan Army; col 3: same as prescribed for Colonel of the Pakistan Army; cols 4–6: Silver colour, embroidered, national emblem on the top, floral circlet with inscription "SPCS" inside. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria with SPCS inscription.

Wreath on Peaked Cap or Pole Cap — Floral embroidered silver-colour wreath on the visor as prescribed for: col 1 Major General; col 2 Brigadier; col 3 Colonel; col 4 Lieutenant Colonel; col 4 (2 years) Major; col 5 Captain; col 6 Lieutenant [?] of the Pakistan Army. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria.

Shirt (Men) — cols 1–6: Cotton, blackish grey Marri cloth shirt, two front pockets on both breasts with plain flaps to buttons, five buttons down the front, shoulder straps, police / military pattern. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria.

Shirt (Women) — cols 1–6: Cotton, blackish grey Marri cloth Frock or Qameez, two front pockets on both breasts with plain flaps to buttons, shoulder straps, removable waist belt with buckle, police / military pattern, long up to knees, design suiting religious /social norms and values. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria.

