Trousers (Men), continued — cols 1–6: ...pockets and one on the back or Khaki Cargo Trousers, two side pockets, two front pockets on thighs, two pockets on the back, may be tucked-in boots at the bottom.

Trousers (Women) — cols 1–6: Shalwar, Grey, Marri Cotton or linen. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria.

Socks — cols 1–6: Plain cotton brown or cotton black without any embroidery work or designing. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria.

Shoes / Boots (Men) — cols 1–6: Long brown /black ammunition boots or Oxford Pattern brown /black shoes with toe and Laces. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria.

Shoes / Boots (Women) — cols 1–6: Black or brown leather walking shoes with laces or Velcro. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria.

Gorget Patches — col 1: Turned down collar with blue Gorget Patches with a silver-colour button at the upper end containing national emblem facing upward, of the same pattern as prescribed for Major-General in Pakistan Army; col 2: same, as prescribed for Brigadier in Pakistan Army; col 3: same, as prescribed for Colonel in Pakistan Army; cols 4–6: Not authorized. — cols 7–11: Not Authorized.

Formation Sign — cols 1–6: Embroidered, silver-colour, floral circlet with inscription "SPCS" and national emblem on the top on a round circle with upper half red and lower half blue to be worn on left arm above elbow three inches below the shoulder line. — cols 7–11: same embroidered formation sign (as above).

Name Plate — cols 1–6: Plastic or metal with sky blue /black background and name in one word (only), written in white/ silver colour in capital letters (only). — cols 7–11: same (plastic or metal, sky blue/black background, name in one word, white/silver capital letters).

Medals / Ribbons — cols 1–6 (and 7–11): According to length of service and as admissible to the civil armed forces, police and rangers, etc.

Shoulder title — cols 1–3: Nil; cols 4–11: SPCS.

Shoulder Ranks — col 1: Silver, metal, crossing sword and baton on both shoulder flashes below one diamond shaped pip as prescribed for Major-General of the Pakistan Army; col 2: Silver, metal, national emblem above three diamond shaped pips arranged in an equilateral triangle on both shoulder flashes as prescribed for Brigadier of the Pakistan Army; col 3: Silver, metal, national emblem above two diamond shaped pips on both shoulder flashes as prescribed for Colonel of the Pakistan Army; col 4: Silver, metal, national emblem above one diamond shaped pip on both shoulder flashes as prescribed for Lieutenant Colonel of the Pakistan Army; col 4 (2 years): Silver, metal, national emblem on both shoulder flashes as prescribed for Major of the Pakistan Army; col 5: Silver, metal, three diamond shaped pips on both shoulder flashes as prescribed for Captain of the Pakistan Army; col 6: Silver, metal, two diamond shaped pips on both shoulder flashes as prescribed for Lieutenant of the Pakistan Army. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria.

Belt — cols 1–3: Sam Browne leather or nylon police belt, black or brown, brass fittings, may be perforated; cols 4–6: same, without perforations. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria.

Belt Plate / Badge — col 1: Rectangular, silver / steel, national emblem on the top, floral circlet, crossing sword and baton inside; cols 2–3: Rectangular, silver / steel, floral circlet crescent containing a five-corner star inside, matching the cap badge; cols 4–6: Rectangular, silver / steel, national emblem on the top, floral circlet with inscription "SPCS" inside. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria.

Swagger Stick — cols 1–3: Malacca cane; cols 4–6: Cane covered with brown or black leather, chrome caps on both ends, inscription "SPCS" at one end cap. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria.$k6p161t$, 1.0, 642, $k6p161b$[{"bbox": [54.0, 100.0, 558.0, 141.133], "text": "553    THE SINDH GOVT. GAZETTE MAY, 14,2020    PART-I", "html": "", "label": "Text", "raw_label": "OwnerTranscription", "script": "latin", "confidence": 1.0, "error": false, "skipped": false, "owner_supplied": true, "block_no": 0, "reading_order": 0, "geometry": "approximate: one block per transcribed line, spaced evenly in reading order"}, {"bbox": [54.0, 142.133, 558.0, 183.267], "text": "Trousers (Men), continued — cols 1–6: ...pockets and one on the back or Khaki Cargo Trousers, two side pockets, two front pockets on thighs, two pockets on the back, may be tucked-in boots at the bottom.", "html": "", "label": "Text", "raw_label": "OwnerTranscription", "script": "latin", "confidence": 1.0, "error": false, "skipped": false, "owner_supplied": true, "block_no": 1, "reading_order": 1, "geometry": "approximate: one block per transcribed line, spaced evenly in reading order"}, {"bbox": [54.0, 184.267, 558.0, 225.4], "text": "Trousers (Women) — cols 1–6: Shalwar, Grey, Marri Cotton or linen. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria.", "html": "", "label": "Text", "raw_label": "OwnerTranscription", "script": "latin", "confidence": 1.0, "error": false, "skipped": false, "owner_supplied": true, "block_no": 2, "reading_order": 2, "geometry": "approximate: one block per transcribed line, spaced evenly in reading order"}, {"bbox": [54.0, 226.4, 558.0, 267.533], "text": "Socks — cols 1–6: Plain cotton brown or cotton black without any embroidery work or designing. — cols 7–11: As per Police Criteria.", "html": "", "label": "Text", "raw_label": "OwnerTranscription", "script": "latin", "confidence": 1.0, "error": false, "skipped": false, "owner_supplied": true, "block_no": 3, "reading_order": 3, "geometry": "approximate